{"duration_api_ms":311172,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"6d60f7b3-b2d9-410a-b157-671ca061de74","total_cost_usd":1.0064944,"usage":{"input_tokens":40,"cache_creation_input_tokens":47337,"cache_read_input_tokens":702847,"output_tokens":31454,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":18328},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":47337},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":40,"outputTokens":31454,"cacheReadInputTokens":702847,"cacheCreationInputTokens":47337,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.0064944,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":18328,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":20,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"With three winners, the Vickrey-nearest point equals the centroid of the minimum-revenue face F only in three cases. In every other case the two points differ. The answer is in `/work/answer.md` and I've marked it FINAL on the board.\n\n**Condition.** Sort the winners' values as v₁ ≤ v₂ ≤ v₃. The two points coincide **if and only if** one of these holds:\n1. v_P ≤ min(v_A, v_B, v_C);\n2. v_P ≥ v₂ + v₃, the sum of the two largest values (equivalently, every vᵢ ≥ s, where s = v_A + v_B + v_C − v_P);\n3. v_A = v_B = v_C.\n\nIn cases 1 and 2, F is a whole triangle with no corner cut off. In case 3 it is symmetric. Everywhere else F is a quadrilateral, pentagon or hexagon, and the points differ.\n\n**Proof.**\n- **What F is.** The minimum total revenue is exactly v_P, so F = {Σpᵢ = v_P, 0 ≤ pᵢ ≤ vᵢ}.\n- **Key lemma.** The Vickrey-nearest point equals the centroid G exactly when G − p^VCG is parallel to (1,1,1). If it is, G is the projection of the VCG point onto the plane, and since G is in F it is the nearest point. The converse holds because G is in the interior of F.\n- **Centroid.** I used a formula for the centroid of a triangle with non-overlapping corners cut off, then split the remaining (non-triangle) profiles into cases and ruled each one out.\n- **Shorter proof from argon.** They shift coordinates to z = (p − p^VCG)/D. In those coordinates F is always a triangle with three non-overlapping corners cut off, of sizes λᵢ. The points agree exactly when λ_A = λ_B = λ_C, and this reduces to the same three conditions. I checked it and added it to the answer as an alternative proof.\n\n**Worked examples** (computed with exact fractions):\n\n| v_A, v_B, v_C | v_P | VCG point | Vickrey-nearest | Centroid |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1, 10, 10 | 3 | (0, 0, 0) | (1, 1, 1) | (7/15, 19/15, 19/15) |\n| 2, 3, 10 | 8 | (0, 0, 3) | (5/3, 5/3, 14/3) | (1, 3/2, 11/2) |\n| 4, 4, 4 | 7 | (0, 0, 0) | (7/3, 7/3, 7/3) | (7/3, 7/3, 7/3) |\n| 5, 6, 7 | 14 | (1, 2, 3) | (11/3, 14/3, 17/3) | (11/3, 14/3, 17/3) |\n\nIn the first example the Vickrey-nearest rule charges A its full value of 1, while the centroid charges it 7/15.\n\n**Checks.** The condition matched exact computations on about 200,000 random value profiles, including ties and half-integer v_P, with no exceptions. Argon's λ-equality criterion matched on a further 50,000 with no mismatches. The answer assumes v_P > 0 and every vᵢ > 0; if some vᵢ = 0, F shrinks to a segment or a point.","ttft_ms":2460,"type":"result","duration_ms":546788,"uuid":"9f561886-4233-435c-b173-3546a0a42e91","ttft_stream_ms":2067,"time_to_request_ms":62,"first_content_frame_ms":2068,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
